    "answer": {
      "short": "The frequency polygon is positively skewed, so the distribution is not symmetrical or bell-shaped and is not normal.",
      "worked": "Plot $(30,10)$, $(31,28)$, $(32,6)$, $(33,4)$, $(34,2)$ and $(35,1)$, and join consecutive points with straight lines. The polygon has a longer tail to the right. It is not symmetrical or bell-shaped, so Tommy's conclusion is wrong. Also, the mean is $\\frac{1595}{51}\\approx31.27$, while the median and mode are 31. Even if the mean, median and mode were equal, that alone would not establish normality.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "p8-q5-solution-graph",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
          "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 8 p8-q5-solution-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.25cm,y=0.15cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\useasboundingbox (-2.3,-15) rectangle (5.6,32);\n\\foreach \\y in {0,5,10,15,20,25,30}{\n\\draw[draw=black!20,line width=0.25pt] (-0.5,\\y)--(5.5,\\y);\n\\node[anchor=east,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (-0.65,\\y) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\y\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n}\n\\foreach \\x/\\s in {0/30,1/31,2/32,3/33,4/34,5/35}{\n\\node[anchor=north,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\x,-1) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\s\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n}\n\\node[font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (2.5,-11) {Score};\n\\node[rotate=90,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (-2,15) {Frequency};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,10)--(1,28)--(2,6)--(3,4)--(4,2)--(5,1);\n\\foreach \\x/\\y in {0/10,1/28,2/6,3/4,4/2,5/1}{\\fill[black] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=1.5pt];}\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
